# MO-1306 Phase 3C targeted refresh

**Independent offline audit complete; ready for Phase 3D evidence integration. Final release certification remains pending the named external gates.**

Baseline: initially clean `mo1306/phase3c-refresh`, C3AB `9e1bbff99c23cdbc4c80f11e87eadb89a36e8f44`, parent C3A `90b9ac914e477fb90fe317d0de9ba310aae37f60`. C3A has B2 `0e35ffe70919d77b1db530929093826410b805f9` as its sole parent; B2 binds I2 `58b7b8cc90fe798fafe6d09bf04db45ceea29f6d`.

Independent corrected archive rebuild: **197172 bytes**, SHA-256 `2f1e9424ce64e44b7b1587ce206fe5f7ae72579652ca1fc891c489bc1a21925d`, exactly **94 regular members** matching current package bytes. Node **24.21.0 x64**, SHA-256 `ba4e6d110e8c1592a1ecd390f6b05f3da124b13871a5be62b341a07a853c6c32`. This audit changes no production bytes and does not substitute for 3B-R installed/supply-chain certification.

## Original blocker and correction

All four uncommitted files in the original 3C worktree retain their initial byte lengths/SHA-256 and match the correction's preserved copies. Original `constructor`, `toString`, and `__proto__` failures remain **BLOCKED / PRODUCTION_DEFECT**, exit 16. The correction creates new evidence; it never rewrites the original outcome.

Fresh correction checks: **228/228**, including **44 native invalid command cases** (20 prototype names plus 24 general invalid inputs) with exact `MO1306_USAGE`/10 and empty stdout. Paired exact-main-source instrumentation proves zero command-handler and installation entry. Native output alone is not represented as instrumentation. Eight inherited getter mutations cannot create commands; three own-command shadows remain valid; three removed-guard controls reproduce the defect. Public run/verify passed native execution. An independent public generate command also exited 0 with empty streams and two files exactly matching independent generation, using the documented detached/closed-stdin launch profile.

Independent dispatch review inventories **135 JavaScript sites**, including 34 high-risk sites, and parses five PowerShell sites. Provider adapter/core/metadata user selectors reject `PROVIDER_UNSUPPORTED`/10; five legitimate providers pass. Internal metadata normalization receives six fixed literal provider call sites. Projection rejection remains the frozen `INTERNAL_FAILURE`/16, distinct from unsupported-provider errors. No second substantive production selector defect was found.

SDK **1.1.0** remains the sole production semantic authority. All 25 authoritative runtime closure members match source bytes. SDK and CLI engineering oracles match normative bytes; no CLI/REST/MCP production fallback or policy-semantic change was introduced. All 28 machine errors, truncation, stable SDK passthrough, first-failure ordering and semantic 0/6/7 versus operational 10-17 separation are checked.

