Fresh provider checks are 454 assertions (376 negatives), 201 GitLab/Jenkins parser tests, 538 Node regression tests and 50 Azure/GitHub API checks. These counts overlap corpus subsets and are deliberately not summed into a single certification total. Source/validator/schema/runtime identities are retained with each scope. Native layer 6 uses explicitly byte-bound unchanged fixed-launcher/core execution evidence and current corrected-entry execution; it is not represented as a new full hosted or installed campaign.

## Security and evidence

Security checks comprise 101 independent cases, 109 targeted logic cases, 152 existing contract tests, 37 worker/network-boundary tests, 14 Correction A contract tests, three exact-source lifecycle traces and 12 trace-negative controls. Fourteen bundle tamper cases and 84 stable SDK-code cases are subsets of 109. The targeted verifier-logic harness substitutes only the PowerShell path helper so helper startup cannot mask intended bundle errors; production filesystem checks and complete native bundle verification are tested separately.

Filesystem coverage includes 43 relative and 21 absolute negative paths, containment, traversal, drive-relative/UNC/device/ADS, hardlinks, native junctions/reparse points and file symlinks, temporary ownership, artifact basenames and incomplete completion markers. Environment coverage includes NODE_OPTIONS/NODE_PATH, preloads/loaders, inspect/debug flags, proxies, credentials, PATH/PATHEXT and unexpected inheritance. The observed child environment is only SystemRoot/WINDIR. Network evidence covers the frozen API/import/permission boundary; no OS-wide firewall or kernel-isolation claim is made.

Correction A topology, direct argv, fixed PowerShell execution, sampled descendants and cleanup are replayed against 92 unchanged package dependencies. No arbitrary shell or Groovy service was introduced. Installed current-artifact resource/cleanup certification remains external 3A-R. YAML, Groovy, PowerShell, GitHub/Azure expressions, multiline/control, metadata, placeholders, paths and output/annotation injection are covered by provider and shared corpora.

All evidence/result/canonical digest and cardinality cross-links are source-bound; tampered results, repaired outer hashes, wrong runs, missing markers, modified normative bytes and extra files reject. Partial metadata-publication output was independently SDK-verified only for normative invariance and remains an incomplete operational failure.

## Preserved attempts and reuse

The original partial 3C parser/schema/transport observations are retained with 142 exact B2/current byte dependencies. Fresh provider outputs and unfinished areas receive current checks. Historical observations are not added to fresh counts, and original failed CLI dispatch is never relabeled PASS. B1's unmodified 152-case suite was replayed; all 2400 retained B2 evidence files and 169 correction evidence files match committed Git blobs. Failed first 2D gate, source 2A/2B, original/corrected 2C, I2/B2 and C3A/C3AB dispositions remain unchanged.

Three security operational refusals and a harness serialization failure remain retained. A valid helper was independently observed near the frozen 2000 ms startup limit; the exact cause of the later metadata publication refusal was not externally traced. Both optional current native GitHub-wrapper attempts also remain failures. The wrapper test launch profile omitted the documented DEVNULL stdin setting; its retry reached operational publication/filesystem refusal followed by transport-integrity rejection. Missing closed stdin and measured helper pressure are supporting setup observations, not a proven immediate cause or a product PASS. No further blind replay was made.

The initial correction-validator replay exceeded its 120-second engineering deadline. The same assertion functions subsequently passed using one independently hash-checked Git cat-file batch instead of hundreds of separate immutable-blob subprocesses. No assertion or production timeout was weakened. Parser/reporting-only setup failures and their corrected harness bytes remain explicit.

