## Validation, commit and Phase 3D notes

Correction binding validator: 8 negative controls. Dispatch validator: 16. Provider validator: 8. Security summary validator: 7. Root audit/matrix validator: 25. Historical lifecycle negative controls: 12. Counts are separate scopes. Workspace verification and git diff --check pass; final staging and commit-parent checks are performed after evidence sealing.

Audit files and their exact executed, initially uncommitted harness hashes are bound by one audit-only commit with subject `cert(memoryos-1.3): audit corrected MO-1306 provider security and release readiness`, parent exactly `9e1bbff99c23cdbc4c80f11e87eadb89a36e8f44`. This document does not invent that future commit's hash. The final validation references the already-created inventory without a self-hash cycle; the actual commit binds both.

Audit evidence preparation elapsed 1900 seconds from 2026-09-26T19:19:55Z, within the 90-minute target and 3-hour absolute stop. No merge, push, tag, Linux/Ubuntu/WSL, local VM, provider account or paid service operation occurred.

Phase 3D must bind actual independent refresh commits, preserve every failed attempt and original 3C blocker, close installed native/resource/cleanup and actual hosted evidence or explicit owner disposition through 3A-R, and close corrected package/SBOM/provenance/advisory acceptance through 3B-R. Use the documented detached/closed-stdin native launch profile; do not promote the failed optional wrapper probes. Final release claims and any tag/push require their separately authorized gates. This audit introduces no release-governance semantics or production corrections.

